await sends "set a to y" to another thread, then sets a to (promise a)
(do a) -> (do (promise y))
but can't do promise y, need to wait for y
block and give the runtime a hook for "queue this when a is written to"
then the runtime requeues (do a)

eval keeps an arg stack
it gets new sexps from evaluated ones
the dispatcher calls eval using the call stack as program counter

send exec path to dispatcher N
or send it to scheduler
scheduler is implemented in userspace, it uses send to dispatcher N itself

